The generated packs in generated/ are made by .kodex/scripts/generate_packs.py from published,
permissively licensed connector schemas. SOURCES.json lists every repository they are made from,
with its URL, licence, commit and the packs it contributes to; the licence texts are in the
repository's licenses/ directory (Apache-2.0.txt, and ontology-pack-sources.txt for each repository
under the MIT licence, with its copyright notice). No Airbyte connector is read: Airbyte's
repository is under the Elastic License 2.0.

- Fivetran's dbt packages (https://github.com/fivetran, the dbt_* repositories), Copyright Fivetran
  Inc., licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Table and column names, the tables their
  staging models read, the columns and values of their test seeds, and the table and column
  descriptions used as entity and measure definitions (from models/**/src_*.yml and the doc blocks
  in models/**/*.md), edited for spelling and punctuation.

- dlt's verified sources (https://github.com/dlt-hub/verified-sources), by dltHub, licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0. Resource names, primary keys and declared columns.

- Singer and Meltano taps whose repositories are licensed under the MIT or Apache-2.0 licences, as
  SOURCES.json lists them with each repository's own licence. Stream names, primary keys, property
  names and types, and property descriptions, edited for spelling and punctuation.

- meltano/hub (https://github.com/meltano/hub), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  which source system each tap reads, and its label.

- The word list of dwyl/english-words (https://github.com/dwyl/english-words), released into the
  public domain (the Unlicense): only to tell apart the words of a name run together, such as
  transactionline. No text of it is in the packs beyond those words.

The hand-written packs in this directory are part of Konstruct (MIT).
